{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"aba673f5beaaf3fa4353d71848d39b7ebacbcf02"},"timestamp":1560442301,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0NTU4MzA3MDQ=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3478","origin":"github"},"title":"Error creating sibling due to keyring","message":"#### What is the problem?\n\nI'm trying to create a sibling and repeatedly fall into this:\n\n```Text\n$ datalad create-sibling-github --github-organization \"templateflow\" --github-login oesteban --dataset tpl-MNIPediatricAsym tpl-MNIPediatricAsym\n[WARNING] Failed to query keyring: a bytes-like object is required, not 'list' [ciphers.py:update_into:140]\n[ERROR  ] a bytes-like object is required, not 'list' [ciphers.py:update_into:140] (TypeError) \n```\n\nThat happened with pip-installed datalad-0.10 \u0026 NeuroDebian's git-annex-standalone and also with conda installed datalad-0.11.5 \u0026 conda installed git-annex (2019X)\n\n#### What steps will reproduce the problem?\nRunning the command line stated above\n\n#### What version of DataLad are you using (run `datalad --version`)? On what operating system (consider running `datalad wtf`)?\n```\n## datalad\n  - full_version: 0.11.4\n  - version: 0.11.4\n## dependencies\n  - appdirs: 1.4.3\n  - boto: 2.49.0\n  - cmd:annex: 7.20190219-g728228d5d\n  - cmd:git: 2.17.1\n  - cmd:system-git: 2.17.1\n  - cmd:system-ssh: 7.6p1\n  - exifread: 2.1.2\n  - git: 2.1.11\n  - gitdb: 2.0.5\n  - humanize: 0.5.1\n  - iso8601: 0.1.12\n  - keyring: 16.0.2\n  - keyrings.alt: 3.1\n  - msgpack: 0.5.6\n  - mutagen: 1.41.1\n  - requests: 2.20.1\n  - six: 1.11.0\n  - tqdm: 4.32.1\n  - wrapt: 1.10.11\n## system\n  - distribution: debian/buster/sid\n  - encoding:\n    - default: utf-8\n    - filesystem: utf-8\n    - locale.prefered: UTF-8\n  - max_path_length: 291\n  - name: Linux\n  - release: 4.15.0-47-generic\n  - type: posix\n  - version: #50-Ubuntu SMP Wed Mar 13 10:44:52 UTC 2019\n```\n\n#### Is there anything else that would be useful to know in this context?\nWriting the password with the ``--github-passwd`` command seemed to work out.\n\n#### Have you had any success using DataLad before? (to assess your expertise/prior luck.  We would welcome your testimonial additions to https://github.com/datalad/datalad/wiki/Testimonials as well)\nYes, very successfully. Thanks for working this great piece of software.","files":null}]}